## Starting a report

**Reports → New report**, then pick the child. Only children in your class are offered — if the
list comes back empty, that's a class-assignment problem rather than a missing report.

Then choose the shape of the report:

- **Weekly** or **Monthly**.
- The **period** it covers.

## The generated draft

**Generate draft** writes a first version for you from the activities already recorded for that
child in that period. This is why recording activities as you go matters: the draft is only as good
as what's there to draw on, and a period with nothing logged produces very little.

{% callout type="warning" %}
The draft is a starting point, not a finished report — the app tells you as much when it produces
one. **Read and edit it before saving.** It's assembled from your activity records, so it can
misjudge tone, repeat itself, or state something more confidently than you would. Nothing reaches
a parent until you publish it, and what they read is whatever you left in the text.
{% /callout %}

You can also skip generation entirely and write from scratch, and you can **add sections** to
structure the report however your setting prefers.

## Draft or published

Two separate buttons, and the difference matters:

- **Save draft** — keeps your work, stays private to staff. Come back and finish it later.
- **Publish** — releases the report to the parent.

Save a draft whenever you're interrupted. Publish only when the report is genuinely ready, since
publishing is what makes it visible outside the staff room.

